      modelAnswerHtml: 'The magic circle, previously a symbol of Prospero\'s supernatural authority, becomes the physical boundary he must dissolve before reconciliation with his enemies can occur. By externalising an internal, moral decision as concrete stagecraft, Shakespeare lets a theatre audience watch Prospero\'s transformation happen rather than simply hear it described.',
      markingGuidanceHtml: 'Look for reference to the symbolic function of the circle specifically (not just "stage directions show emotion"), and an explanation of why drama benefits from externalising an internal change this way.',
